      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Title: SkyLink CLI \"Quick Start Guide\"\n\nWelcome to the SkyLink CLI \"Quick Start Guide.\" This document aims to help you quickly deploy your development environment with the SkyLink CLI tool.\n\nPrerequisites:\n- The latest version of Docker is installed on your machine.\n- Node.js version 18 or above is installed.\n\nInstallation:\n1. Open your terminal.\n\n2. Run the following command to install SkyLink CLI globally using `npm`:\n```\nnpm install -g skylink-cli\n```\n\nBuild confirmation:\nEnsure that the installation was successful by verifying the SkyLink CLI version:\n```\nskylink --version\n```\n\nAuthentication:\n1. Sign in using the `skylink login` command, which will provide a prompt to enter your username and password.\n\n2. The welcome message will confirm your authentication status.\n\nDeployment:\nTo deploy to a staging environment, follow these steps:\n1. In your terminal, type `skylink deploy --env staging` to start the deployment process.\n\n2. Monitor the deployment progress in the terminal, and once it's finished, you will receive a success confirmation message.\n\n3. You can also run `skylink status --env staging` to check the current status of your deployment in",
      "source": "target",
